items: v2-unknown-member-on-a-builtin-receiver-yields-a-closure-instead-of-refusing
paths: file:v2/src/Runtime.scala file:tests/e2e/v2-unknown-member-refuses-gate.sh file:scripts/smoke-ci.ssc file:v2/runtime/std/json-plugin/src/main/scala/ssc/plugin/json/NativeJsonCodec.scala
scope: |
  A bare `recv.name` on a builtin receiver has no nullary dispatch and becomes the eta-expansion
  closure, so a name that exists nowhere printed `<closure>` and exited 0. Stopped where the value
  would ESCAPE (rendering), not at dispatch, because the fallback is load-bearing — measured: the
  reference refuses the bare selection even for a method that EXISTS, while v2 answers `true` for
  `List("b","z").exists("abc".contains)`. Runtime half landed in 2e7ad72dc.
  WIDENED to the json codec BEFORE editing it: NativeJsonCodec renders every ClosV as the JSON
  string "<function>", so the same typo can still reach an HTTP body — the rozum `{"cell":{Stub}}`
  shape one sentinel over. Same one-arm fix, plus a row in the gate.
next: json codec arm + gate row, rebuild, smoke, land; then file the entry in v2/BUGS.md once its
  current holder releases it
